1
00:00:08,674 --> 00:00:12,263
The Buddha told a wandering
ascetic named Bahiya:

2
00:00:12,343 --> 00:00:15,279
in the seen, there will be just the seen.

3
00:00:15,359 --> 00:00:18,341
No one behind the eyes, doing the seeing.

4
00:00:19,153 --> 00:00:23,054
Nāgārjuna, in chapter three
of his Fundamental Verses,

5
00:00:23,134 --> 00:00:26,695
says: without a seer, there is no seen.

6
00:00:26,775 --> 00:00:29,607
And without the seen, there is no seer.

7
00:00:30,413 --> 00:00:33,689
Many people are confused when
they hear these two together.

8
00:00:33,769 --> 00:00:35,672
The Buddha takes the seer away.

9
00:00:35,752 --> 00:00:39,939
Nāgārjuna seems to put it back,
and then tie it to the seen.

10
00:00:40,019 --> 00:00:42,833
So they see a contradiction.
There is none.

11
00:00:42,913 --> 00:00:44,681
One is the direct insight.

12
00:00:44,761 --> 00:00:49,970
The other is how the logic of dependency
expresses that same insight and taste.

13
00:00:50,793 --> 00:00:55,907
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

14
00:00:56,725 --> 00:01:01,088
I want to make this as plain as I can,
because everything after anatta turns on

15
00:01:01,168 --> 00:01:03,927
it. It also answers a second question.

16
00:01:04,007 --> 00:01:08,995
When I tell people that, to me, dependent
arising is spontaneous presence,

17
00:01:09,075 --> 00:01:10,340
they ask why.

18
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:15,829
How can the hard logic of Nāgārjuna lead
to something as effortless as spontaneous

19
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:20,046
presence? It is the same answer,
carried one step further.

20
00:01:20,849 --> 00:01:22,961
Start with how we usually talk.

21
00:01:23,091 --> 00:01:26,448
"I see the tree." There
is someone here, the seer.

22
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:28,472
There is something there, the tree.

23
00:01:28,553 --> 00:01:32,535
And there is an act that crosses
the gap between them, the seeing.

24
00:01:32,615 --> 00:01:36,086
Subject, verb, object. Three parts.

25
00:01:36,909 --> 00:01:39,451
That shape feels like
a fact about the world.

26
00:01:39,531 --> 00:01:41,557
It is a fact about sentences.

27
00:01:41,637 --> 00:01:46,081
A sentence holds a subject still,
so that the verb can happen to it.

28
00:01:46,161 --> 00:01:49,872
The habit runs so deep
that we feel it must be so.

29
00:01:49,952 --> 00:01:52,168
Every action needs someone doing it.

30
00:01:52,248 --> 00:01:54,003
Every seeing needs a seer.

31
00:01:54,083 --> 00:01:56,249
This is the logic of substance.

32
00:01:56,352 --> 00:01:59,465
Things are there first,
finished and on their own.

33
00:01:59,545 --> 00:02:01,806
Then they act, and are acted on.

34
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:07,849
We say "the wind blows", as if there were
a wind first, and then it did the blowing.

35
00:02:07,929 --> 00:02:13,012
But when the blowing stops, no wind
is left over, resting somewhere.

36
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:16,056
The blowing is the
wind. Keep this in mind.

37
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:19,783
Everything that follows does the
same thing to something else.

38
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:25,340
Bahiya was told to drop that shape,
not by arguing, but by looking.

39
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:27,473
In seeing, just the seen.

40
00:02:27,553 --> 00:02:30,204
When this is tasted, it is very plain.

41
00:02:30,284 --> 00:02:32,745
There is the tree, vivid and bright.

42
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:36,617
Look for a seer standing
behind it, and none is found.

43
00:02:36,697 --> 00:02:38,329
The seeing has no centre.

44
00:02:38,409 --> 00:02:44,013
This is the insight of anatta, no
self. It is not a theory. It is direct.

45
00:02:44,817 --> 00:02:47,155
It is exact to say what falls away.

46
00:02:47,235 --> 00:02:49,139
The person does not fall away.

47
00:02:49,219 --> 00:02:54,628
You still have a name, catch the bus,
keep your promises. Seeing does not stop.

48
00:02:54,708 --> 00:02:56,449
It is brighter than before.

49
00:02:56,529 --> 00:03:00,851
What falls away is one picture:
someone standing behind the action,

50
00:03:00,931 --> 00:03:03,776
making it happen. A doer behind the doing.

51
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:07,044
But insight is not yet understanding.

52
00:03:07,124 --> 00:03:10,509
Many who have tasted it keep the
old grammar in their thinking.

53
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:15,386
They say "there is no seer", and still
picture a subject that went missing,

54
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:17,356
a gap where it used to be.

55
00:03:17,436 --> 00:03:21,487
Or they turn the seer into
a big, impersonal awareness,

56
00:03:21,567 --> 00:03:24,766
and the subject is back,
wearing a larger coat.

57
00:03:25,577 --> 00:03:27,929
This is where Nāgārjuna comes in.

58
00:03:28,009 --> 00:03:30,062
He does not give a new experience.

59
00:03:30,142 --> 00:03:32,671
He shows why the old grammar cannot hold.

60
00:03:32,751 --> 00:03:38,078
In the substantialist framework, an
action must always be started by an agent.

61
00:03:38,158 --> 00:03:40,470
Nāgārjuna is refuting that.

62
00:03:40,550 --> 00:03:42,335
Many think he is affirming it.

63
00:03:43,149 --> 00:03:47,444
Watch how he argues. He takes the
logic of substance at its word.

64
00:03:47,524 --> 00:03:50,311
You say a seer is there, on its own side.

65
00:03:50,391 --> 00:03:53,562
Very well: is that seer seeing, or not?

66
00:03:54,361 --> 00:03:57,460
If it is not seeing, in
what sense is it a seer?

67
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:01,269
A seer that does not see
is a seer in name only.

68
00:04:02,069 --> 00:04:05,576
If it is seeing, then the
seeing is counted twice.

69
00:04:05,656 --> 00:04:09,316
Once to make it a seer, and once
more for the seeing it does.

70
00:04:10,137 --> 00:04:14,187
So the seer is not found with
seeing, and not found without it.

71
00:04:14,267 --> 00:04:19,894
In his words: there is no seer, either
bound up with seeing or apart from it.

72
00:04:19,974 --> 00:04:21,592
Then he turns to the seen.

73
00:04:21,672 --> 00:04:25,030
A thing is only "seen"
in relation to seeing.

74
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:28,607
Take seeing away, and
nothing is left that is seen.

75
00:04:29,413 --> 00:04:33,794
Now read his verse again:
without a seer, there is no seen.

76
00:04:33,883 --> 00:04:38,468
He is not saying, "there is a
seer, and it leans on the seen."

77
00:04:38,557 --> 00:04:42,892
He is saying the seer cannot stand
on its own. Neither can the seen.

78
00:04:42,972 --> 00:04:45,787
Each is named only in
relation to the other.

79
00:04:45,867 --> 00:04:49,133
Take away the relation,
and neither is left over.

80
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:51,786
That is not a seer put back.

81
00:04:51,866 --> 00:04:56,487
It is the seer taken apart, inside
the very grammar that made it.

82
00:04:56,567 --> 00:05:02,425
So how does "no seen without a seer,
no seer without the seen" become

83
00:05:02,505 --> 00:05:04,780
"in the seen, just the seen"?

84
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:08,050
Nāgārjuna does not remove
a seer that was there.

85
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:12,796
He shows that "seer" was only ever
a name for one side of the seeing.

86
00:05:13,618 --> 00:05:16,718
Take away the colours,
the shapes and the light,

87
00:05:16,798 --> 00:05:20,291
and look for what is left over
that was the seer. Nothing.

88
00:05:20,371 --> 00:05:23,484
Just as "wind" adds
nothing to the blowing,

89
00:05:23,564 --> 00:05:26,437
"seer" adds nothing to the seeing.

90
00:05:27,281 --> 00:05:29,312
Think of "here" and "there".

91
00:05:29,455 --> 00:05:32,731
"Here" makes sense only
in relation to "there",

92
00:05:32,811 --> 00:05:35,734
and "there" only in relation to "here".

93
00:05:35,814 --> 00:05:40,313
Look for "here" by itself, and
it is not a place you can stand.

94
00:05:40,393 --> 00:05:44,905
The seer is like that "here": the
point the scene seems to be seen from.

95
00:05:44,985 --> 00:05:49,760
Seen through, there is no "here" behind
the view. There is just the view.

96
00:05:50,586 --> 00:05:53,699
This is how the Buddha goes
on in his teaching to Bahiya.

97
00:05:53,779 --> 00:05:58,006
When in the seen there is just
the seen, there is no "you" in it.

98
00:05:58,086 --> 00:06:02,313
Then you are neither here, nor
there, nor anywhere in between.

99
00:06:02,393 --> 00:06:04,881
The Buddha says it from the direct taste.

100
00:06:04,961 --> 00:06:09,773
Nāgārjuna gives the logic for it:
here and there are named together,

101
00:06:09,853 --> 00:06:12,060
so neither is found by itself.

102
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:15,718
And this is why the
verse must run both ways.

103
00:06:15,862 --> 00:06:20,184
"Just the seen" is easy
to misread: the seer gone,

104
00:06:20,264 --> 00:06:22,725
and an object out there left standing.

105
00:06:22,805 --> 00:06:26,692
That is still the logic of
substance, with one side missing.

106
00:06:26,772 --> 00:06:29,464
But there is no seen
without the seer either.

107
00:06:29,544 --> 00:06:33,336
So "just the seen" is
the appearing itself,

108
00:06:33,416 --> 00:06:37,059
vivid and complete, with
nothing standing behind it,

109
00:06:37,139 --> 00:06:39,287
and nothing standing apart from it.

110
00:06:39,367 --> 00:06:44,061
Seer, seeing and seen are three ways
of speaking about one appearing.

111
00:06:44,882 --> 00:06:47,954
So many readers get Nāgārjuna backwards.

112
00:06:48,034 --> 00:06:51,161
They hear "seer and seen
depend on each other",

113
00:06:51,241 --> 00:06:54,843
and picture two solid
things, joined by a thread.

114
00:06:54,923 --> 00:06:57,737
But "depend" here does
not join two things.

115
00:06:57,817 --> 00:07:00,454
It shows there were never
two things there to join.

116
00:07:00,534 --> 00:07:02,796
This is the logic of dependency.

117
00:07:03,617 --> 00:07:06,173
Chapter three is not a special case.

118
00:07:06,253 --> 00:07:09,868
Nāgārjuna makes the same
move again and again.

119
00:07:09,948 --> 00:07:14,610
Each time he takes something that seems
to stand behind an action, doing it.

120
00:07:14,690 --> 00:07:19,148
Each time he asks: is it the same
as the action, or other than it?

121
00:07:19,228 --> 00:07:21,313
Each time it is found as neither.

122
00:07:22,125 --> 00:07:26,501
In chapter two, the walker and
walking. A goer does not go.

123
00:07:26,581 --> 00:07:32,303
Not because nobody walks, but because
"walker" and "walking" are not two things,

124
00:07:32,383 --> 00:07:33,843
one doing the other.

125
00:07:34,657 --> 00:07:37,702
In chapter three, the seer and seeing.

126
00:07:37,782 --> 00:07:42,190
There is no seer, either bound
up with seeing or apart from it.

127
00:07:43,013 --> 00:07:45,446
In chapter ten, fire and fuel.

128
00:07:45,526 --> 00:07:50,392
If fire were the fuel, the one who
acts and what is acted on would be one.

129
00:07:50,472 --> 00:07:54,242
If it were other than the fuel,
it could exist without fuel.

130
00:07:54,371 --> 00:07:57,584
Fire is not a thing that
arrives and grabs the wood.

131
00:07:58,414 --> 00:08:02,601
And chapter one goes furthest of
all: the cause and its effect.

132
00:08:02,681 --> 00:08:06,337
Not from itself, not from
another, not from both,

133
00:08:06,417 --> 00:08:08,171
and not without a cause.

134
00:08:08,251 --> 00:08:10,386
It takes the doer out of causes.

135
00:08:10,466 --> 00:08:14,109
A cause does not stand there
first and then make its effect,

136
00:08:14,189 --> 00:08:16,328
the way a factory makes goods.

137
00:08:17,149 --> 00:08:18,903
So the two teachings meet.

138
00:08:18,983 --> 00:08:23,441
Anatta finds no doer in seeing,
and it finds this by looking.

139
00:08:23,521 --> 00:08:27,707
Nāgārjuna finds no doer
anywhere: in the walker,

140
00:08:27,787 --> 00:08:30,737
the fire, the cause, the seen.

141
00:08:30,817 --> 00:08:32,531
He finds this by reasoning.

142
00:08:32,611 --> 00:08:35,533
One shows that no seer
is found when we look.

143
00:08:35,613 --> 00:08:39,614
The other shows why no seer
could be found, however we look.

144
00:08:40,433 --> 00:08:42,513
It did not happen by itself for me.

145
00:08:42,593 --> 00:08:45,380
Anatta dawned around 1997.

146
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:49,918
But for years afterwards my experience
and insight were non-substantialist,

147
00:08:49,998 --> 00:08:51,657
while my view was not.

148
00:08:51,737 --> 00:08:55,244
In experience, the taste
was implicitly non-dual.

149
00:08:55,324 --> 00:08:57,717
But when the mind tried to understand it,

150
00:08:57,797 --> 00:09:02,268
it could not, because its logical
thought was always substantial.

151
00:09:02,348 --> 00:09:05,855
Insight without the logic
drifts back into nouns,

152
00:09:05,935 --> 00:09:10,964
and the seer returns as a witness,
a ground, a vast awareness.

153
00:09:11,044 --> 00:09:15,190
Logic without insight stays a
clever argument about words.

154
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:18,210
Only together do the
view and the taste agree.

155
00:09:19,042 --> 00:09:24,152
We must understand why "found as
neither" is emptiness. Take a car.

156
00:09:24,232 --> 00:09:28,949
If "car" pointed to something that
stands on its own, we could point to it.

157
00:09:29,029 --> 00:09:33,541
It could be the parts. It could be
a whole, over and above the parts.

158
00:09:33,621 --> 00:09:36,856
Or it could be their shape.
No single part is the car.

159
00:09:36,936 --> 00:09:39,180
All the parts in a box are not a car.

160
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:43,650
Take every part away, and no car
is left over to be the whole.

161
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:47,087
And the shape is only the
parts in a certain relation.

162
00:09:47,167 --> 00:09:50,076
Candrakīrti asks the same of the chariot:

163
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:53,804
the same as its parts, or
other than them? Neither.

164
00:09:54,638 --> 00:09:58,000
These are all the places a car
standing on its own could be.

165
00:09:58,117 --> 00:10:01,433
Found in none of them, it
has no nature of its own.

166
00:10:01,513 --> 00:10:04,178
That not-finding is what "empty" means.

167
00:10:04,258 --> 00:10:06,664
Not that the car is made of emptiness.

168
00:10:06,744 --> 00:10:10,781
And emptiness is not something
left over once the parts are gone.

169
00:10:10,861 --> 00:10:15,487
Only that, looked for on its own
side, there is nothing there to find.

170
00:10:16,301 --> 00:10:18,232
And still the car drives you home.

171
00:10:18,312 --> 00:10:22,253
The search looked for one thing
only, a car from its own side.

172
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:24,509
It never touched the car that works.

173
00:10:24,589 --> 00:10:26,751
Looked for, it is not found.

174
00:10:26,831 --> 00:10:29,916
Met, it is there, doing what cars do.

175
00:10:29,996 --> 00:10:31,669
These are not two facts.

176
00:10:31,749 --> 00:10:35,922
That is why Nāgārjuna can say that
dependent arising is what we call

177
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,202
emptiness.

178
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:40,803
The seer is the same.
The same as the seeing?

179
00:10:40,883 --> 00:10:44,132
Then "seer" adds nothing. Apart from it?

180
00:10:44,212 --> 00:10:45,953
Then it is nowhere to be found.

181
00:10:46,033 --> 00:10:48,412
Neither, so the seer is empty.

182
00:10:48,492 --> 00:10:50,369
The seen gets the same test.

183
00:10:50,449 --> 00:10:52,339
What is left is not a remainder.

184
00:10:52,419 --> 00:10:55,061
It is the seeing, vivid and complete.

185
00:10:55,874 --> 00:11:00,536
The seer and seen are named together,
and the car is named in dependence on its

186
00:11:00,616 --> 00:11:04,504
parts. This is not a label stuck
on something already there,

187
00:11:04,584 --> 00:11:06,840
like "sugar" written on a jar.

188
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:10,251
Naming here is picking
something out as "this",

189
00:11:10,331 --> 00:11:13,715
in the appearing itself, before any words.

190
00:11:13,795 --> 00:11:15,826
There is nothing bare underneath it.

191
00:11:16,638 --> 00:11:19,778
There is one more step,
and it is easy to miss.

192
00:11:19,858 --> 00:11:23,451
Once the seer is gone, the
mind wants to keep something:

193
00:11:23,581 --> 00:11:26,979
"Fine, no seer. Just seeing, then."

194
00:11:27,059 --> 00:11:31,056
But a verb can be made into
a thing as easily as a noun.

195
00:11:31,136 --> 00:11:36,844
If "seeing" becomes a stream, a process,
a field that everything happens in,

196
00:11:36,924 --> 00:11:38,637
the substance is back.

197
00:11:38,717 --> 00:11:41,739
It has only moved from
the subject to the verb.

198
00:11:42,562 --> 00:11:45,431
So the seeing, too, is looked for.

199
00:11:45,511 --> 00:11:51,164
Apart from the colour, the light, the
eye and the tree, where is it? Not found.

200
00:11:51,244 --> 00:11:55,567
Seer, seeing and seen are
named together, on conditions.

201
00:11:55,647 --> 00:11:57,306
None is found on its own.

202
00:11:57,386 --> 00:12:02,537
In Nāgārjuna's words, dependent
arising is what we call emptiness.

203
00:12:02,617 --> 00:12:07,242
That is a designation in dependence,
and that itself is the middle way.

204
00:12:08,078 --> 00:12:11,259
There is one more place the
mind likes to hide something.

205
00:12:11,339 --> 00:12:15,702
It comes most of all to practitioners
who taste that appearances are one's own

206
00:12:15,782 --> 00:12:19,914
clarity. The sound is not out
there, heard by someone in here.

207
00:12:19,994 --> 00:12:24,873
The sound itself is clear, itself
the knowing. The taste is genuine.

208
00:12:24,953 --> 00:12:28,460
But read with the old logic,
it turns into a conclusion:

209
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:32,418
everything is made of one
stuff, and that stuff is mind.

210
00:12:33,234 --> 00:12:36,252
The physical world can
seem to point the same way.

211
00:12:36,332 --> 00:12:38,902
Weight feels like the most
private thing there is.

212
00:12:38,982 --> 00:12:42,421
But weight is a pull between
the body and the earth.

213
00:12:42,501 --> 00:12:44,309
On the Moon it is a sixth.

214
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:48,141
In orbit it is gone, and
not a gram of you is lost.

215
00:12:48,221 --> 00:12:52,652
Ernst Mach argued that even the body's
resistance to being pushed comes from its

216
00:12:52,732 --> 00:12:55,940
relation to all the
matter in the universe.

217
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:59,513
So where is the line between
my body and the world,

218
00:12:59,593 --> 00:13:02,652
in the heaviness itself? It is not found.

219
00:13:02,732 --> 00:13:05,994
Matter turns light, magical and plastic.

220
00:13:06,074 --> 00:13:10,659
And it is easy to take one more
step, and say: so it was all mind.

221
00:13:11,494 --> 00:13:14,499
But in Buddhism everything
is a phenomenon,

222
00:13:14,579 --> 00:13:18,507
mind and matter alike, and the
knowing is on that list too.

223
00:13:18,587 --> 00:13:22,311
The Buddha says consciousness
is named after its condition,

224
00:13:22,391 --> 00:13:25,137
as a fire is named after what it burns.

225
00:13:25,217 --> 00:13:27,411
Nothing knows from outside the list.

226
00:13:28,226 --> 00:13:31,054
So mind cannot be the ground of the rest.

227
00:13:31,134 --> 00:13:35,130
It is on the list, not under
it, and it meets the same test.

228
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:37,684
There is no hearing apart from the sound,

229
00:13:37,764 --> 00:13:39,722
the ear and the attention.

230
00:13:39,802 --> 00:13:43,187
Both mind and matter are vivid, both work,

231
00:13:43,267 --> 00:13:45,728
and neither is found from its own side.

232
00:13:45,808 --> 00:13:50,134
Making matter the floor and making
mind the floor are the same mistake.

233
00:13:51,026 --> 00:13:53,324
"Own clarity" does not mean owned.

234
00:13:53,404 --> 00:13:58,433
The clarity is the appearance's own,
not lent to it by a knower behind it.

235
00:13:58,513 --> 00:14:00,607
Mind-like is not made of mind.

236
00:14:00,687 --> 00:14:04,017
If everything is my mind, or the one Mind,

237
00:14:04,097 --> 00:14:07,128
then appearances belong
to someone after all,

238
00:14:07,208 --> 00:14:10,063
and the owner is back in
the largest coat of all.

239
00:14:10,143 --> 00:14:14,402
Appearing is clear and complete,
and it belongs to no one.

240
00:14:15,213 --> 00:14:17,211
Now the point everything depends on.

241
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:19,032
There are two ways to say no.

242
00:14:19,112 --> 00:14:22,773
One way says no, and then puts
something else in its place.

243
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:26,564
"There is no small self, so
there must be a big Self."

244
00:14:26,707 --> 00:14:30,160
"There is no seer, so there
must be pure awareness."

245
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:35,191
Each time, the doer leaves by the front
door and comes back by the back door.

246
00:14:36,001 --> 00:14:38,801
Nāgārjuna's no is the other kind.

247
00:14:38,881 --> 00:14:41,152
It removes, and adds nothing.

248
00:14:41,232 --> 00:14:44,317
The tradition calls it a
non-implicative negation:

249
00:14:44,397 --> 00:14:47,932
it denies, without implying anything else.

250
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:51,029
No seer, and nothing in the seer's place.

251
00:14:51,109 --> 00:14:54,739
No producing cause, and
nothing producing instead.

252
00:14:54,819 --> 00:14:57,646
Even dependence is not
kept as a new thing.

253
00:14:57,726 --> 00:15:02,442
The conditions are not a web or a
machine standing behind what appears.

254
00:15:02,522 --> 00:15:05,993
They, too, are not found
from their own side.

255
00:15:06,797 --> 00:15:11,785
Now go back to the wind. If no wind
stands behind the blowing, pushing it,

256
00:15:11,865 --> 00:15:14,054
the blowing is not being done.

257
00:15:14,134 --> 00:15:17,251
It is simply the blowing,
complete as it is.

258
00:15:18,057 --> 00:15:22,148
Widen that to everything. If nothing
makes the sound of a car going by,

259
00:15:22,228 --> 00:15:24,050
the sound is not a product.

260
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:26,618
It is not waiting for
anything to finish it.

261
00:15:26,698 --> 00:15:31,238
It shows up whole and vivid,
exactly as its conditions meet.

262
00:15:31,318 --> 00:15:35,748
If nothing makes the thought, the
thought appears and goes by itself.

263
00:15:35,828 --> 00:15:38,497
No one has to hold it, or push it away.

264
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:41,734
That is what spontaneous presence means.

265
00:15:41,814 --> 00:15:47,033
Appearing is already complete, because
nothing is hidden behind it, doing it.

266
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:52,251
It is the last of the seven phases:
presence is spontaneously perfected.

267
00:15:52,331 --> 00:15:56,232
Not a new state reached at the
end, but how it always was,

268
00:15:56,312 --> 00:15:58,704
once the doer is gone everywhere.

269
00:15:58,784 --> 00:16:02,622
As I put it: anatta is
a seal, not a stage.

270
00:16:03,438 --> 00:16:05,587
This is also why it is effortless.

271
00:16:05,667 --> 00:16:09,513
It is not difficult to see,
especially in meditation.

272
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:12,665
There is an energetic
openness and release,

273
00:16:12,745 --> 00:16:17,326
as if everything is in its
own self so, without an actor.

274
00:16:17,406 --> 00:16:22,914
That lets us understand that holding,
pushing and managing are the agent itself:

275
00:16:23,058 --> 00:16:27,122
one happening split into
two, a doer and its doing,

276
00:16:27,202 --> 00:16:31,184
through a confusion that language
and its structure lead us into.

277
00:16:31,264 --> 00:16:35,333
When no doer is found anywhere,
there is no one left to push.

278
00:16:36,154 --> 00:16:37,940
Two cautions keep this right.

279
00:16:38,737 --> 00:16:41,456
Spontaneous does not mean uncaused.

280
00:16:41,536 --> 00:16:44,621
The car still has to go by
for its sound to appear.

281
00:16:44,701 --> 00:16:48,901
Conditions still come together,
and the world still follows them.

282
00:16:48,981 --> 00:16:51,677
What is gone is the maker, not the order.

283
00:16:52,493 --> 00:16:55,619
And spontaneous presence is not a source,

284
00:16:55,699 --> 00:16:58,255
a ground that gives off appearances.

285
00:16:58,335 --> 00:17:00,837
That would bring the doer back once more,

286
00:17:00,917 --> 00:17:02,906
in its most beautiful coat.

287
00:17:03,705 --> 00:17:09,114
So when I say that dependent arising is
spontaneous presence, this is what I mean.

288
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:12,320
They are one appearing,
described in two ways.

289
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:16,206
Dependent arising is how it
is described when we analyse.

290
00:17:16,286 --> 00:17:21,478
Spontaneous presence is the same
appearing when the habit of fixing stops:

291
00:17:21,558 --> 00:17:25,051
complete, effortless,
with nothing behind it.

292
00:17:25,131 --> 00:17:27,135
Neither description is higher.

293
00:17:27,962 --> 00:17:32,325
One thing must be said plainly here,
or all of this can be misheard.

294
00:17:32,405 --> 00:17:34,282
Clarity is never missing.

295
00:17:34,362 --> 00:17:37,488
You cannot talk about
phenomena without clarity.

296
00:17:37,568 --> 00:17:39,336
A sound is clear as sound.

297
00:17:39,416 --> 00:17:41,374
A colour is vivid as colour.

298
00:17:41,454 --> 00:17:43,494
A thought is known as it appears.

299
00:17:43,574 --> 00:17:47,461
Dependent arising is never a
machine working in the dark,

300
00:17:47,541 --> 00:17:49,730
waiting for a knower to light it up.

301
00:17:49,810 --> 00:17:51,895
The clarity is always there.

302
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:55,715
So the question is never
whether there is clarity.

303
00:17:55,795 --> 00:18:00,524
It is only whether the clarity is
abstracted out and made into a thing.

304
00:18:00,604 --> 00:18:05,538
Clarity shows up in every sight,
every sound, every thought.

305
00:18:05,618 --> 00:18:08,894
The mind notices this
sameness and lifts it out:

306
00:18:08,974 --> 00:18:13,323
awareness, presence, the one thing
that is there in all of them.

307
00:18:13,403 --> 00:18:16,421
Then it takes that abstraction
to stand on its own.

308
00:18:16,501 --> 00:18:19,791
It becomes the background
that everything appears in,

309
00:18:19,871 --> 00:18:24,465
the witness that knows it all, the
Mind that gives off appearances.

310
00:18:24,545 --> 00:18:27,657
The substrate is back,
now made of clarity.

311
00:18:27,737 --> 00:18:31,774
It is the same move that makes the
chariot a thing over its parts,

312
00:18:31,854 --> 00:18:33,137
done to the knowing.

313
00:18:33,957 --> 00:18:37,301
Left as it is, the
clarity is not lifted out.

314
00:18:37,381 --> 00:18:41,173
It stays the appearing's
own: this sound's clearness,

315
00:18:41,253 --> 00:18:44,719
this colour's vividness,
found only as them,

316
00:18:44,799 --> 00:18:46,431
and on their conditions.

317
00:18:46,511 --> 00:18:48,800
It is not a second thing the sound has.

318
00:18:49,622 --> 00:18:53,944
The same lifting out, done to
other things, is the same mistake.

319
00:18:54,024 --> 00:18:58,646
Abstract the conditions, and you get
a web or a machine behind the world.

320
00:18:58,726 --> 00:19:02,110
Abstract the appearing, and
you get an object out there.

321
00:19:02,190 --> 00:19:05,371
Abstract emptiness, and you get a ground,

322
00:19:05,451 --> 00:19:08,713
a field, a space everything sits in.

323
00:19:08,793 --> 00:19:11,988
Dependent arising undoes all of these.

324
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:14,108
It does not take the clarity away.

325
00:19:14,188 --> 00:19:17,047
It only stops it from
being made into a thing.

326
00:19:17,874 --> 00:19:22,101
When nothing is abstracted, nothing
stands behind the appearing:

327
00:19:22,181 --> 00:19:25,688
no maker, no knower, no background.

328
00:19:25,768 --> 00:19:29,058
Without a substrate,
appearing presents itself,

329
00:19:29,138 --> 00:19:33,976
clear by itself and complete by
itself, as its conditions meet.

330
00:19:34,056 --> 00:19:36,087
That is spontaneous presence.

331
00:19:36,897 --> 00:19:38,950
None of this takes anything away.

332
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:40,607
The tree is still green.

333
00:19:40,687 --> 00:19:43,352
You still read road
signs and catch a ball.

334
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,879
Because nothing is
there from its own side,

335
00:19:45,959 --> 00:19:48,787
things can change, meet and work.

336
00:19:48,867 --> 00:19:53,302
If a seer were truly fixed, it could
never learn to see differently.

337
00:19:53,418 --> 00:19:57,550
"I see the tree" can stay, as
a convenient way of speaking.

338
00:19:57,630 --> 00:19:59,738
That shape is useful for talking.

339
00:19:59,818 --> 00:20:02,079
It is not the shape of what appears.

340
00:20:02,893 --> 00:20:06,671
In one line: anatta
finds no doer in seeing.

341
00:20:06,751 --> 00:20:11,902
Nāgārjuna finds no doer anywhere,
and puts nothing in its place.

342
00:20:11,982 --> 00:20:17,609
With no doer anywhere, and the clarity
not lifted out and made into a thing,

343
00:20:17,689 --> 00:20:21,563
everything appears clear
and complete, by itself,

344
00:20:21,643 --> 00:20:23,333
as its conditions meet.

345
00:20:24,137 --> 00:20:26,462
Try it now. Look, or listen.

346
00:20:26,542 --> 00:20:30,103
A colour, a car, a fan, a voice.

347
00:20:30,183 --> 00:20:32,970
Notice it, vivid, just as it is.

348
00:20:33,050 --> 00:20:37,875
Then look for the one who is seeing
or hearing. Do not argue. Just look.

349
00:20:37,955 --> 00:20:40,660
Now look for the seeing
apart from what is seen.

350
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:44,030
Look for something that makes
it happen. Nothing is found.

351
00:20:44,110 --> 00:20:46,068
Do not put anything in its place.

352
00:20:46,148 --> 00:20:48,939
Let it be as it is, already complete.

353
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:51,517
What is left is not a blank.

354
00:20:51,597 --> 00:20:56,517
It is the scene, bright and
whole, coming and going by itself,

355
00:20:56,597 --> 00:21:00,529
with no one standing behind it,
and nothing standing under it.

356
00:21:01,345 --> 00:21:04,598
In seeing, just the
seen. Now you know why.

